---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /vocab/themes/index.html
title: European security studies research themes
description: The seventeen-theme controlled vocabulary the Anthology indexes by, in English, French and German, published as SKOS.
navKey: "navigator"
lang: en
ccbyLicence: true
---
{#- The concept scheme's own URI has to resolve, the same way each concept's
    does (#1249). This is that page, and it is the one a citation points at.
    Everything on it comes from themeVocab.js, so a label fix lands here and in
    both serialisations at once. -#}
<header class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Vocabulary</span>
    <h1>{{ themeVocab.title }}</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      The seventeen research themes the
      <a href="/anthology.html">Anthology</a> indexes by, each with a permanent
      identifier and a label in English, French and German.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="card" style="padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-7));">
      <p>
        Nine of the themes are the permanent sections of the European Security
        Studies Conference. The other eight recur across the open panels. Every
        concept identifier below resolves, and each theme's own view in the
        <a href="/anthology-atlas.html">Atlas</a> lists the papers it tags.
      </p>
      <p>
        The whole vocabulary as SKOS:
        <a href="/vocab/themes.ttl">Turtle</a> or
        <a href="/vocab/themes.jsonld">JSON-LD</a>.
        Reusable under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">CC BY 4.0</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

{%- for tier, heading in {"permanent": "Permanent conference sections", "derived": "Recurring themes from the open panels"} %}
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>{{ heading }}</h2>
    <ul>
      {%- for concept in themeVocab.concepts %}{% if concept.tier == tier %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ concept.pages.en }}">{{ concept.prefLabel.en }}</a>
        <span class="muted">— {{ concept.prefLabel.fr }} · {{ concept.prefLabel.de }}</span><br>
        <code>{{ concept.uri }}</code>
        <span class="muted">({{ concept.count }} papers)</span>
      </li>
      {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}
